201.m:
And Saṅkarṣaṇa with the seed-syllable 'Ā', and Pradyumna in the south;
[Page 238]
Aniruddha with 'Aḥ' in the southwest, and Nārāyaṇa with 'Oṃ' in the water [quarter, the west];

202.m:
likewise, atimukta; pāṭalā grants the realm of Viṣṇu;
[Page 240]
with karavīra blossoms one goes to Viṣṇu's realm, and with javā flowers one becomes meritorious;
